; ============================================================ ; ; the eight initial hash words  unless the caller
                                                               ; brought its own SHA_384 and both of the SHA_512/t
                                                               ; variants are THIS CORE with a different eight  so a
                                                               ; caller that wants one writes H itself and raises the
                                                               ; flag at
; @0x21a; The flag is NOT spent  because HMAC enters this routine three times
                                                               ; over and all three of them want the same answer; A
                                                               ; caller that leaves it at nought gets SHA_512  which
                                                               ; is every caller that existed before this line; to the
                                                               ; flag
